// # oodar/scripts — Build, Test, Verify, Release Entry Points
//
// Logline: The v2.2.0+ scripts/ subdir holds the build, verify, and reproducible-build entry points. The canonical single-TU build is `gcc oodar.c`; the Makefile adds a `liboodar.a` static library artifact; the repro_build.sh script produces a bit-identical liboodar.a across builds.
//
// Setup: Per RFC-0005, the canonical four scripts are build, test, verify, and release. The v2.2.0+ surface covers build (Makefile) and verify (repro_build.sh); test is in qa/; release is via the governance workflow per RULES.oot §1.24.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Makefile       — builds liboodar.a from the umbrella TU (or, as a best-effort alternative, per-file).
//   2. repro_build.sh — reproducible build with SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, deterministic ar, sorted input, sha256 hash, verify mode.
//
// ──▓▓ oodar/scripts ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: Makefile (225 lines) + repro_build.sh (246 lines) — both <= 256 ::
